%% Runtime — one interactive booking run (section 6.1)
%% Diagrams as code. Render with any Mermaid renderer.
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant L as Launcher
    participant P as Pipeline
    participant PL as paperless-ngx
    participant S as Staging
    participant B as Book process
    participant G as GnuCash desktop

    U->>L: start (instead of gnucash)
    L->>L: backup book (file copy, or pg_dump)
    L->>B: export corpus, CoA, existing, SX definitions (READ_ONLY)
    B-->>P: JSON
    L->>P: run
    P->>PL: list new statements, fetch originals (?version=)
    P->>P: parse, balance check, normalise, dedup, correlate
    P->>PL: bill metadata for the batch window
    P->>P: link bills, classify, disposition, batch gate
    P->>S: stage proposals
    alt batch gate refuses
        P-->>L: refusal
        L->>U: notify
    else rows to review
        L->>U: open review file in $EDITOR (gated rows pre-marked a)
        U-->>L: saved = approval of rows marked a
        L->>P: strict parse by ID
        P->>S: approve / correct / reject
        Note over L,B: until build step 5 the run stops here: decisions recorded, nothing written
        L->>B: apply approved rows (NORMAL_OPEN)
        B->>B: drop rows whose ID is already a num
        B->>B: create / split / match_existing, set doc link
        B->>B: session.save()
        B->>B: post-apply assertions
        B->>B: read-back confirms each row
        B-->>S: proposal_id, tx_guid, status
        L->>L: remove review file
    end
    L->>G: exec gnucash (always)
